<title>USA: SubMicron extends exchange offer.</title>
<headline>SubMicron extends exchange offer.</headline>
<dateline>ALLENTOWN, Pa. 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>SubMicron Systems Corp said on Monday it has extended until 1700 EDT September 6, 1996, its exchange offer for holders of its nine percent convertible subordinated notes due 1997.</p>
<p>The previous expiration date for the debt-to-equity exchange was August 26, the company said.</p>
<p>The offer is for the exchange of the $1,000 in principal of notes and the warrants to buy up to 60 shares at $14 per share in return for 135 shares of common stock.</p>
<p>There are $19 million in principal of these notes outstanding, a company spokesman said.</p>
</text>
